                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "237248976",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198399375565",
                            "num_reviews": 271,
                            "playtime_forever": 599,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 599,
                            "last_played": 1791505872
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Mighty No. 9 is a 2D Action Platformer with Megaman inspiration. You play as robot named \"Beck\" created by Dr. William White and your mission is to neutralize the threat of the other Mighty numbers and the rogue robots in the city.\n\nThe game offers over 10 stages each filled with precision platforming sections and lots of enemies to take down while navigating through each stage. The platforming was average at the first few stages but it gets tougher as you delve deeper into the progression of the game.\n\nThe controls were pretty tight as well as the movement and attacking of the character, I didn't face a single bug or issue during my playthrough.\n\nI enjoyed lots of megaman games during my childhood and this one is definitely up there. The stages design and the powers you obtain by defeating the other mighties will definitely come into play in late game and it will be crucial to bypass some stages and sections.\n\nOST and music were nostalgic as it brought the sweet childhood memories of megaman days. Enjoyable to listen to while taking down enemies across multiple stages.\n\nThe boss battles were a real highlight, some definitely will keep you on your toes to nail down those dashes before the bosses regen their HP or whether it's dodging or jumping over a dangerous attack.\n\nIt's really recommended if you're a big fan of megaman games or 2D Action Platformers in general.\n\nOverall Rating 9/10",
                        "timestamp_created": 1791507639,
